From 8241b2d741e2ad93dabe67a37934efe7ff8e37cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:44:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] refactor(linalg)!: remove Matrix.rankSvd(), now covered
 by rank()

`Matrix.rank()` is SVD-based by default, so `rankSvd()` duplicates it.
Remove the public method (it was added in the same unreleased series); the
algorithm stays as an internal helper that `rank()` calls.

Validation errors raised from the shared SVD code now name the public
routine that was called (`Matrix rank`, `Matrix cond2`, `Matrix
singularValues`) instead of always saying `singularValues`. The SciPy
benchmark compares `rank()` instead of `rankSvd()`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Lt4LXANr7M53RsCeDAwAGm
